The digit sum is 0x7 + 0xd + 0xc + 0x9 = 0x29, whose final hexadecimal digit <code>9</code> falls in the <code>8</code>-<code>f</code> range.
The result was announced at 17:08 UTC on 2026-08-11 -- "7+D+C+9 = 29 / 9 = BLAKE2b" -- selecting BLAKE2b-256, the algorithm specified in this document.
<ref>[https://x.com/LukeDashjr/status/2087224739265687685 Drawing result: "7+D+C+9 = 29 / 9 = BLAKE2b" (17:08 UTC)]</ref>

The final draw's design addressed the first drawing's ambiguity.
Aggregating over every block in the window removes any dependence on which competing block counts as "first" -- the same burst production that broke the first drawing occurred again, harmlessly.
And the override clause prefers the expensive-to-grind mainnet beacon whenever one exists.

===== Lessons learned from the drawings =====

The failed first stages demonstrated concretely that a fair public drawing requires a pre-committed candidate list and procedure, and a randomness beacon that is expensive to bias and yields a unique result -- achieved in the final draw by salted commitments that concealed even the procedure itself until after the fact, aggregation over an unpredictable window, and the mainnet-block override.

=== Activation ===

Mining with BLAKE2b began on 2026-08-30, when the New York Post published the front page bearing the [[#Activation_headline|activation headline]].
Block 961,639 was the final SHA256d block.

Activation was unanimous and did not split the chain:
no valid SHA256d block was produced after height 961,639, so no chain continued under the previous rules.

=== Retargeting after activation ===

The activation block, at height 961,640 on 2026-08-30, had a difficulty of about 130 P, set by the [[#Activation_target_adjustment|activation target adjustment]].
Hash rate grew gradually from about 0.6 Ph/s, and the remaining 2,008 blocks of that retarget period were mined in about 2.4 days.
<ref name="retarget-blocks">Figures are derived from the timestamps and targets in the block headers.
The linked retarget blocks can be viewed, for example, at [https://mempool.guide/block/0000000000000050c1e5f69672f459293be14f46e5a494e7a8c8541396f18eeb mempool.guide].</ref>

As expected, the first retarget after activation, at height 963,648, made the target easier:
the period it measured began at height [https://mempool.guide/block/0000000000000000000169eb6f811ddbd0daf343af7b62180cdb13e7c78dbc16 961,632] on 2026-08-08, so most of it elapsed while SHA256d block production was nearly stalled.
The difficulty fell by about 41.3%, and with hash rate steady at about 2.4 Ph/s, the next 2,016 blocks took only about 17.5 hours.
The following retargets raised the difficulty by the maximum factor of four, while hash rate rose only slowly, to about 3.5 Ph/s.

Less expected, several periods after activation, BLAKE2b hashing hardware that had been mining BLAKE2b-based altcoins joined.
Between 2026-09-05 and 2026-09-12, hash rate rose from about 4 Ph/s to about 30 Ph/s.
<ref name="retarget-blocks" />
Two more retargets by the maximum factor of four, and one of about 2.99, were needed to catch up:

